    PCI: qcom: Add link retention support (v3 patches 2/4 + 3/4, PORTED)

    Link retention series v3 patches 2/4 ("Keep PERST# GPIO state as-is
    during probe") and 3/4 (core link_retain logic), not merged upstream as
    of 2026-09. The series was authored against a pcie-qcom.c that had the
    qcom_pcie_parse_perst()/parse_ports() refactoring which postdates v6.19;
    this file ports both patches onto the v6.19 pcie-qcom.c:

      - parse_perst -> qcom_pcie_parse_port() (devm_fwnode_gpiod_get site)
      - parse_ports' perst -> qcom_pcie_parse_legacy_binding()
        (devm_gpiod_get_optional site)
      - qcom_pcie_perst_assert/deassert -> qcom_ep_reset_assert/deassert
        (guarded in qcom_pcie_host_init)
      - host_init err path: no pci_pwrctrl_* labels in v6.19, the
        preserve-on-EPROBE_DEFER check sits at the qcom_pcie_phy_power_on
        error branch instead
      - struct dw_pcie_rp: link_retain added after native_ecam (v6.19
        lacks skip_l23_ready/skip_pwrctrl_off)

    From (v3 series):
      https://marc.info/?l=linux-kernel&m=178357909997412&q=raw (2/4)
      https://marc.info/?l=linux-kernel&m=178357909697404&q=raw (3/4)
    (lore message-ids 20260709-link_retain-v3-{2,3}-81a9d187bb61@oss.qualcomm.com)

